  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Saturday)\nIssued at 1112 AM MDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nSW CONUS upper trough will direct copious amounts of Pac moisture\nand embedded impulses over the Rockies and into the region. This \nwill support a decent chance of showers and storms for much of the\nFA, best chances over the SD Plains. Stronger northern stream \ntrough will then force a stronger cold front into the region Wed \nnight, supporting a brief cool down. Moisture filled SW flow aloft\nwith embedded impulses will continue to support rounds of showers \nand TS chances through Monday as low level Gulf moisture spreads \nwest. Lead pos theta-e adv continues to support elevated showers \nand storms in the far eastern FA with a few light showers across \nscentral SD. LL moist easterly upslope flow continues to support \nwidespread cloud cover over much of the western SD Plains, except\nfor far NW SD. The next impulse will arrive later tonight and \nsupport another round of rain chances, mainly after midnight, with\nmore isolated chances before given lack of appreciable forcing. \nNorthern CONUS impulse will force a sfc trough into the FA Monday.\nThis feature will provide the focus for afternoon/evening showers\nand storms, esp on the SD Plains where deeper low level moisture \nwill be in place. Isolated strong to severe cells are possible as \nflow increases aloft with the approaching upper level trough, esp \nacross NW SD. Rain chances will shift east overnight with things \ndrying out Tues. Expect seasonal temps to continue after today \nwith highs in the 70s most places through Wed. Deeper upper trough\nwill advect across southern Canada and support a stronger cold \nfront into the region by Wed night. This will allow for much drier\nand cooler air to shift south across the Northern Plains, with \nmuch cooler weather for Thur. However, this will be short lived as\nshortwave ridging is expected for the end of the week, bringing \nwarmer but continued seasonal 